    "Punchline": "Deep Ducking public host and authenticated module access.",
    "Description": "The Deep Ducking public host provides the introduction, community links and authenticated loading of separately supplied DDuck modules. /dd and /dduck open the introduction when no module is loaded.\n\nFull module required for all commands below except opening the host window.\n\nCommands (all /dd commands also accept /dduck):\n/dd [toggle main window]\n/dduck [alias for /dd; accepts all commands below]\n/dd mini [toggle Mini]\n/dd settings [open Settings]\n/dd config [open Settings]\n/dd debug [open Advanced]\n/dd help [open command help]\n/dd start [floor] [start or continue selected save; optional fresh-run floor]\n/dd party-start [floor] [alias for start]\n/dd party [select fixed-party POTD while idle]\n/dd adopt [bind eligible already-entered party dungeon]\n/dd hold [pause local output; retain run for Resume]\n/dd resume [resume retained local run after readiness checks]\n/dd nextstop [exit after next boss]\n/dd ns [exit after next boss]\n/dd stop [FULL STOP; persist local lock across reloads; stay in duty]\n/dd reset-stop [clear eligible FULL STOP after cleanup; do not start]\n/dd status [print local status]\n/dd inspect [record read-only client and native observations]\n/dd saves [open Saves]\n/dd saves info <dungeon> [inspect native saves]\n/dd saves delete <dungeon> <1|2> [delete selected save after native checks; no extra confirmation]\n/dd saves dof <dungeon> <1|2> <on|off> [set future-failure deletion preference; no deletion now]\n/dd saves cancel [cancel pending save or Start preparation; completed actions remain]\n\nDungeon arguments: potd, hoh, eo, pt. [floor] is optional; <...> is required. Choose one value for 1|2 or on|off; omit brackets when typing. Start can replace stopped state; Resume can release an eligible retained in-dungeon run. nextstop and ns retain the save and keep Mini open until return is observed; repeat to confirm the same request. Use the existing boss-break button to cancel.",
